==English==
{{wikipedia|Two pence (British decimal coin)}}

===Etymology===
{{surf|en|two|pence}}, collective plural of [[penny]].

Same for the definition: "{{ellipsis of|en|tuppence worth||one’s opinion}}" however, this idiom is derived from this fact; in Britain it used to cost two pence ("tuppence") to post a letter, usually holding one's opinion.

